    "media:imagetext": "HOW TO LAUNCH AND INFLATE RAFTS\nCEILING RAFT COMPARTMENTS\n1. To open ceiling raft com-\npartment, pull this handle\ndown.\n2. Lift raft off compartment\ndoor and launch out nearest\nexit.\nHOW TO INFLATE RAFTS\nWhen raft is launched into water it\nis secured to the airplane by a tape.\n25 MAN RAFT\naa unas un\nTo avoid inflating the raft inside the\nairplane do not lift or drag the raft by\nthis flap.\nTo inflate raft in the water lift this\nflap and pull ring and cable all the\nway out.\nINFLATED RAFT\nAutomatic life raft radio\nbeacon. Rescue units can\nlocate your raft hundreds\nof miles away by means\nof this radio.\nSURVIVAL\nEQUIPMENT\nIN HERE\nA boarding ramp can be\nextended by pulling this\nRED tab.\nHeaving line. Quickly\nthrow this lifeline to peo-\nple in the water who need\nhelp to reach the raft.\nKNIFE\nFEDERAL AVIATION REGULATIONS REQUIRE:\nDURING TAKE OFF AND LANDING YOUR SEAT BACK AND TRAY TABLE MUST BE\nIN THE UPRIGHT POSITION AND YOUR CARRY-ON LUGGAGE PLACED UNDER A SEAT",
