    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "OVERWATER\nFOR YOUR SAFETY. Know how to move\nSUPER DC-8\nout of this airplane fast. There is fire-danger\n****\nany time a landing is other than normal—partic-\nularly when the airplane structure is damaged.\nBelow is a floor plan of the plane you are in. Familiarize yourself with the location of\nthe exits. Note particularly the exits nearest you. Study how they are opened and also\nthe protective position you should assume during an emergency landing. When leav-\ning, do not take coats, purses or baggage with you. Move to the exits immediately.\nA WORD ABOUT YOUR SEAT BELT-Rough air (turbulence) at high altitudes,\nalthough infrequent, can be severe. When seat belt sign is lighted in-flight, please\ncomply with the sign immediately to prevent possible injury. Experienced air travel-\ners usually keep their seat belts fastened all the time when seated.\nUNITED\nCOCKPIT\nCA-332\nHOW TO OPEN EXITS\nPRINTENA\nEXIT DOORS WITH SLIDES\nESCAPE EXITS WITH SLIDES\nLift handle up and over-push\nRemove cover-pull handle in\nout on door.\nand down-let go of handle\nwhen exit starts to fall out.\nEXIT\nDOOR\nWITH\nSLIDE\nEXIT\nLOCATION\nAND\nOPERATION\nESCAPE\nEXIT\nWITH\nSLIDE\nESCAPE\nEXIT\nWITH\nSLIDE\nEXIT\nDOOR\nWITH\nSLIDE\nPull red handle\nto inflate slide.\nWhen exit falls out - slide\nis automatically inflated.\nESCAPE\nWINDOWS\nOVER\nWING\nAFTER SLIDE INFLATES-JUMP AND\nSLIDE IN SITTING POSITION\nESCAPE\nEXITS\nWITH\nSLIDE\nESCAPE\nEXITS\nWITH\nSLIDE\nESCAPE WINDOWS OVER WINGS\nPull window handle in and down.\nExit through window-leg, body, leg.\nDiscard window.\nAt rear of wing, slide down flaps.\n0\nEXIT\nDOOR\nWITH\nSLIDE\nEXIT\nDOOR\nWITH\nSLIDE",
      "HOW TO LAUNCH AND INFLATE RAFTS\nCEILING RAFT COMPARTMENTS\n1. To open ceiling raft com-\npartment, pull this handle\ndown.\n2. Lift raft off compartment\ndoor and launch out nearest\nexit.\nHOW TO INFLATE RAFTS\nWhen raft is launched into water it\nis secured to the airplane by a tape.\n25 MAN RAFT\naa unas un\nTo avoid inflating the raft inside the\nairplane do not lift or drag the raft by\nthis flap.\nTo inflate raft in the water lift this\nflap and pull ring and cable all the\nway out.\nINFLATED RAFT\nAutomatic life raft radio\nbeacon. Rescue units can\nlocate your raft hundreds\nof miles away by means\nof this radio.\nSURVIVAL\nEQUIPMENT\nIN HERE\nA boarding ramp can be\nextended by pulling this\nRED tab.\nHeaving line. Quickly\nthrow this lifeline to peo-\nple in the water who need\nhelp to reach the raft.\nKNIFE\nFEDERAL AVIATION REGULATIONS REQUIRE:\nDURING TAKE OFF AND LANDING YOUR SEAT BACK AND TRAY TABLE MUST BE\nIN THE UPRIGHT POSITION AND YOUR CARRY-ON LUGGAGE PLACED UNDER A SEAT"
    ],
